@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.9.5
@changelog
  - Codename: Lock, Step and Gone
  - TotalMix pans that stop on the centre and stay there, ORC's lamp colours on the UF8, and Lock position and Lock size for the focused-track panel.
  - Focused-track panel: Lock position and Lock size in its right-click menu, so a stray drag leaves the floating panel where it is. Greyed out while docked.
  - TotalMix, pan: whole percent, and a stop on the centre on the way to the other side, on the UF1's pot above the fader, the UF8's V-Pots and the channel pages. At a V-Pot speed other than 1.00 a pan could skip from L1 to R1.
  - TotalMix, starting up: a UF1 or UF8 that is switched on or comes back on USB can report turns nobody made. For five seconds after Rea-Sixty picks up a surface its turns do nothing in TotalMix. Keys and a fader under the hand work at once.
  - TotalMix, pan log: every change the UF1 and UF8 make to an output's pan goes into rme_pan.log with the control that made it, a turn ignored while a surface starts up as a line with ignored.
  - TotalMix, lamps: the colours set in ORC 1.8 for SEND/PLUG-IN and the bank keys V-POT and 1-5 show on the UF8 in REAPER too.
  - TotalMix, names: with more than one RME interface, snapshot and layout names come from the settings file of the interface TotalMix shows. Until now the newest file was taken.
